---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';
import AsideNav from '../../components/AsideNav.astro';
const path = '/compliance/environment';
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Compliance', href: '/compliance' },
  { name: 'Environment', href: path },
];
---
<Base
  title="Environment: Balancing Data Security and Recycling"
  description="How to balance data sanitization needs with cost and the environment: when to shred, and when secure erasure lets equipment be recycled or refurbished."
  path={path}
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <PageHero
    crumbs={crumbs}
    eyebrow="Environment"
    title="Environment"
    lead="Balancing data sanitization needs with cost and the environment is one of the trickiest decisions for our partners and clients."
  />
  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="wrap with-aside">
      <article class="prose">
        <p>
          Physical destruction by shredding gives total confidence in data sanitization and eliminates the chance of data recovery.
          After all, what information can you recover from thousands of pieces? At the same time, shredding makes recycling more
          complex and less likely, because it gets in the way of recovering materials further downstream.
        </p>
        <p>
          Environmentally conscious clients may choose secure erasure for storage media that does not hold highly sensitive
          information, so the equipment can be recycled for its materials or refurbished for a second useful life.
        </p>
        <p>
          For example, a customer might choose an erasure method (Secure Erase or Cryptographic Erase) for Apple MacBook Pros from late
          2017 onwards, which have soldered-on storage and memory. The choice there is between physically destroying the entire device's
          circuit boards, or securely erasing the storage drive.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/contact-us">Contact us</a> to find out how we can work together on securing both your data and the future of our
          environment.
        </p>
      </article>
      <AsideNav section="/compliance" path={path} />
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBand />
</Base>
